  "display_title": "To My Dishonest Immortal",
  "description": "A woman forever burdened by misfortune, In Greenwood. Disaster followed her like a shadow, and unhappiness gave her no moment to catch her breath. Each time, in those life-threatening moments, a benefactor appeared to save her. But before they could exchange even a single word of thanks, he would vanish like mist.\n\n\\[Why not test whether meeting him was chance or fate?\\] Then one day, as a train fell from the sky and crushed her—A strange, uncanny man, seemingly not meant to exist in this world, appeared once more and saved her life.\n\n *“Would you at least tell me your name now?”\n\n“Adrian. Call me whatever you like.”*\n\n(Source: Lezhin, translated)",
